From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_sandbox: a jail's capabilities -- the MCP servers,
 skills and connectors its project chose
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo proposal §6.64 step 2 (ask 87), on §6.69's MCP-over-ACP (0149, 0150).
0146 left out of a jailed session every MCP server the jail could not start,
and handed it every one it could, as its command line -- arguments, env and
all. So a jail got a server's API key whenever its binary happened to sit
inside the jail's view, and never got an extension server, whatever the
operator wanted. The operator decided on 2026-11-22 that MCP servers, skills
and plugins reach a jail as chosen per project, servers carrying a secret
listed but off, and claude.ai connectors off unless a project turns them on.

The choice, per project (agent_sandbox.projects[<root>], user file only, as
the rest of the section):
- mcp_servers: the names of Zeo's MCP servers (its context servers, and
  zeo-lsp) the jail may use. Default none: each one reaches outside the jail.
- skills: Zeo's skills (0147) in the jail, default on as in 0.20.0. Off, the
  launch maps neither the plugin root nor ~/.agents/skills, and session/new,
  load and resume send no skills plugin (new_session_meta gains `skills`).
  It is in the settings fingerprint, so the lock says "restart to apply".
- claude_ai_connectors (0146) gets its page switch.

What a jailed session gets (acp.rs, jail_servers.rs): only chosen servers.
A chosen server Zeo runs is proxied when the connection proxies at all (the
agent advertised mcpCapabilities.acp and agent.mcp_servers_over_acp is on:
AcpConnection::proxies_mcp, the gate declare_mcp_servers uses), and is then
kept wherever its files are, since the agent reaches Zeo's copy; 0146's
"outside the jail" filter applies only to the chosen ones that are not
proxied, which keep their notice, now saying why Zeo could not hand them
over. mcp_proxy_policy returns Only(<the project's list>), so zeo-lsp too
reaches a jail only when chosen. An unchosen server is not handed over in any
form (one debug line counts them). The list is read from the settings of now
at every session/new: a choice applies to the next thread without a restart,
and is left out of the fingerprint for that reason. The launch record's key
is looked up as `drifted` does (launch::settings_key_now, renamed from the
private record_settings_key), so a project entry first written after the
start is found.

The page (settings_ui pages/agent_jail_capabilities.rs, new; the jail page
only gains the call): a Capabilities block in This Project, after the limits:
one switch per server of the project's context server store, plus zeo-lsp
while agent.zeo_lsp is on and any chosen name no longer configured (so it can
be turned off), each with its status; the Skills switch; a note that Zeo has
no Claude Code plugin store yet, so a jail gets none of the host's
(~/.claude/plugins is not mapped) and Zeo's skills reach it as plugins; the
connectors switch. Every switch is a Tab stop wrapped by the page's
RevealOnFocus.

Secrets (agent_sandbox capabilities.rs, new): a server whose configuration
looks like it carries one -- a non-empty value under a name containing KEY,
TOKEN, SECRET, PASS(WORD|WD), CREDENTIAL, AUTH (not AUTHOR) or COOKIE, in its
env, a --flag=value or --flag value argument, an http header or URL
parameter, an extension's own settings, a Bearer/Basic value, an OAuth client
secret -- is listed with where ("argument --figma-api-key"), never the value.
Turning it on asks first, Cancel preselected: "Its configuration carries a
secret (...). The secret will be readable inside the jail whenever Zeo hands
the server over instead of proxying it, and the agent can use the server's
access either way." Turning any server off never asks. The writers live
beside confirm.rs's (whose ask/save become pub(crate)) and key the entry the
same way (target_project_key).

Not here: read-only maps of a chosen server's binaries and allow_hosts for a
remote one -- a proxied server needs neither, and one that is not proxied is
left out with the notice when the jail cannot see it; a Claude Code plugin
store (none exists in Zeo).

Tests: agent_sandbox capabilities_tests (the heuristic, hostile lookalikes,
the prompt never quoting a value, Cancel writes nothing, Allow adds, off
never asks, defaults); agent_servers jail_servers_tests (only chosen servers,
a proxied one kept outside the jail's view, a chosen unproxied one still left
out, nothing filtered unjailed) and mcp_over_acp_jail_tests (0150's, now: an
unchosen server reaches a jail in no form, a chosen one is proxied, another
choice opens nothing, skills follow the project); settings_ui
agent_jail_capabilities_tests (rows, secret note and prompt, a removed choice
still listed, zeo-lsp off not offered) and the page's Tab order, which gains
the three Capabilities stops of its fixture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
